 ### [Continuous Stochastic Solids Volume Rendering](18428-continuous-stochastic-solids-volume-rendering.md)
-Continuous Stochastic Solids Volume Rendering is a technique that treats Gaussian primitives as continuous stochastic solids, replacing standard 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) rasterization to improve geometric accuracy and depth synthesis quality. It solves the problem of floating-depth artifacts caused by vanilla 3DGS alpha-blending, which blends foreground and background depths, by allowing transmittance to vary continuously along each ray. Unlike sibling methods such as [2DGS](9154-3d-gaussian-unscented-transform-3dgut.md) which use fixed median-depth selection, this method provides a differentiable, continuous formulation for depth and normal rendering.
